#!/bin/sh
# summary-table <engagement> [--write | <label>=<file> ...]
# Prints the ingestion comparison as a markdown table with one column per transcript, read from the
# Metrics section of each summary (F11), plus a column for the change between the last two.
#   no arguments        every evaluation/Tnnn-summary.md in the engagement, in transcript order
#   --write             the same, written to evaluation/ingestions.md (F12)
#   <label>=<file> ...  the given files as columns, in order (used by bin/summary for a single comparison)
set -e
. "$(dirname "$0")/lib.sh"
[ $# -ge 1 ] || die "usage: summary-table <engagement> [--write | <label>=<file> ...]"
eng=$1; shift; d=$(eng_dir "$eng"); ev="$d/evaluation"
write=0; [ "${1:-}" = "--write" ] && { write=1; shift; }
L=$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/sumt.XXXXXXXX"); trap 'rm -f "$L"' EXIT
if [ $# -eq 0 ]; then
  for f in $(ls "$ev" 2>/dev/null | grep '^T[0-9]*-summary\.md$' | sort); do
    tid=${f%-summary.md}; subj=$(header_field "$d/sessions/$tid/$tid.session.md" 'Meeting subject' 2>/dev/null || true)
    printf '%s%s\t%s\n' "$tid" "${subj:+ $subj}" "$ev/$f" >> "$L"; done
else for a in "$@"; do printf '%s\t%s\n' "${a%%=*}" "${a#*=}" >> "$L"; done; fi
[ -s "$L" ] || die "no ingestion summaries under $ev"

table=$(awk -F'\t' '
  function label(k) { return (k in LB) ? LB[k] : k }
  function comma(v,   s, o, neg) { if (v !~ /^-?[0-9]+$/) return v; neg = (v ~ /^-/); s = neg ? substr(v, 2) : v; o = ""
    while (length(s) > 3) { o = "," substr(s, length(s) - 2) o; s = substr(s, 1, length(s) - 3) }; return (neg ? "-" : "") s o }
  function fmt(k, v) { if (v == "") return "not recorded"
    if (k ~ /_pct$/) return v "%"; if (k ~ /_usd$/) return sprintf("$%.2f", v); return comma(v) }
  BEGIN { n = split("model|Model;ingester_version|Ingester version;rules_version|Rules version;transcript_minutes|Transcript minutes;cues|Cues;utterances|Utterances;speakers|Speakers;elapsed_minutes|Elapsed minutes;active_minutes|Active minutes;s3_minutes|S3 write minutes;waiting_minutes|Minutes waiting on the reviewer;reviewer_messages|Reviewer messages;model_calls|Model calls;output_tokens|Output tokens;cache_read_tokens|Cache read tokens;cache_write_tokens|Cache write tokens;input_tokens|Input tokens (uncached);items|Items drafted;episodes|Episodes;needs_human|Needs a human;human_share_pct|Needs a human share;changed_items|Items the reviewer changed;changed_pct|Share of items changed;confident_changed|Confident items the reviewer changed;citations|Citations;output_tokens_per_item|Output tokens per item;output_tokens_per_100_utterances|Output tokens per 100 utterances;cost_usd|Total cost (API list price);cost_per_item_usd|Cost per dossier item;session_usage_pct|Five-hour session limit used;session_windows|Five-hour windows spanned;weekly_usage_pct|Weekly limit used;s4_elapsed_minutes|S4 elapsed minutes;s4_active_minutes|S4 active minutes;s4_waiting_minutes|S4 minutes waiting on the reviewer;s4_model_calls|S4 model calls;s4_output_tokens|S4 output tokens;s4_cost_usd|S4 cost (API list price);s4_session_usage_pct|S4 five-hour session limit used;s4_weekly_usage_pct|S4 weekly limit used;s4_flows|S4 flows;s4_items|S4 processes items;s4_needs_human|S4 needs a human;s4_changed_items|S4 items the reviewer changed", pairs, ";")
    for (i = 1; i <= n; i++) { split(pairs[i], kv, "|"); LB[kv[1]] = kv[2]; ORD[i] = kv[1] }; nord = n
    while ((getline line < ARGV[1]) > 0) { split(line, c, "\t"); cols++; lab[cols] = c[1]; f = c[2]; on = 0; seenhdr = 0
      while ((getline l < f) > 0) { if (l ~ /^## Metrics/) { on = 1; seenhdr = 1; continue } if (l ~ /^## /) { on = 0; continue }
        if ((on || !seenhdr) && l ~ /^- [a-z_0-9]+: /) { k = substr(l, 3); sub(/:.*/, "", k); v = l; sub(/^- [^:]*: /, "", v); V[cols, k] = v
          if (!(k in LB) && !(k in extra)) { extra[k] = 1; ORD[++nord] = k } } }
      close(f) }
    hdr = "| Metric"; sep = "|---"; for (j = 1; j <= cols; j++) { hdr = hdr " | " lab[j]; sep = sep "|---" }
    if (cols > 1) { hdr = hdr " | Change, " substr(lab[cols - 1], 1, index(lab[cols - 1] " ", " ") - 1) " to " substr(lab[cols], 1, index(lab[cols] " ", " ") - 1); sep = sep "|---" }
    print hdr " |"; print sep "|"
    for (i = 1; i <= nord; i++) { k = ORD[i]; any = 0; for (j = 1; j <= cols; j++) if ((j SUBSEP k) in V) any = 1; if (!any) continue
      row = "| " label(k); for (j = 1; j <= cols; j++) row = row " | " fmt(k, V[j, k])
      if (cols > 1) { a = V[cols - 1, k]; b = V[cols, k]; ch = ""
        if (a ~ /^[0-9.]+$/ && b ~ /^[0-9.]+$/ && a + 0 > 0 && k !~ /version/) ch = sprintf("%+.0f%%", 100 * (b - a) / a); row = row " | " ch }
      if (k ~ /^cost_/) { row = "| **" label(k) "**"; for (j = 1; j <= cols; j++) row = row " | **" fmt(k, V[j, k]) "**"; if (cols > 1) row = row " | **" ch "**" }
      print row " |" } exit }' "$L")

if [ $write -eq 0 ]; then printf '%s\n' "$table"; exit 0; fi
out="$ev/ingestions.md"; ver=0.1; [ -f "$out" ] && ver=$(doc_version "$out" | awk -F. '{ printf "%d.%d", $1, $2 + 1 }')
{ printf '# Ingestion comparison: %s\n\nVersion %s, %s.\n\n' "$eng" "$ver" "$(today)"
  printf 'One column per transcript, from the Metrics section of each `evaluation/Tnnn-summary.md`. Regenerated by `ingester/bin/summary` after every ingestion; do not edit. Each transcript'"'"'s own summary holds its window, stage times, caveats and the detail behind each row. The last column is the change between the two most recent transcripts.\n\n'
  printf '%s\n\n' "$table"
  printf 'Cost is the API list-price equivalent of the tokens, from `ingester/pricing.tsv`; on a Claude subscription plan nothing is charged per token. Time and token figures cover everything in each transcript'"'"'s window, including any other work done in the same session inside it. "Not recorded" means the transcript'"'"'s summary was written before that figure was collected.\n'
} > "$out"
printf 'ingestions: %s (%s transcripts)\n' "$out" "$(grep -c . "$L")"
